    "description": "Missouri Meerschaum Corncob Pipe Lot\n2 Piece Set, Vintage Tobacco Smoking Pipes\nCorncob, Wood, and Plastic, Approximately 6 Inches Long\nA pair of vintage corncob tobacco pipes manufactured by the Missouri Meerschaum Company of Washington, Missouri. Founded in 1869, Missouri Meerschaum is the world's oldest and largest manufacturer of corncob pipes, known for their cool-smoking properties and historical significance in American culture. These two examples feature different bowl textures and stem designs, ideal for collectors or enthusiasts of traditional smoking implements.\nLot includes two distinct corncob pipes with wooden stems and amber-toned mouthpieces\nOne pipe retains the original factory label on the base identifying it as a Missouri Meerschaum original\nHandcrafted construction utilizing natural corncob for a unique porous smoking experience\nSizes range from approximately 5.5 to 5.75 inches in total length\nCondition:\nBowls show evidence of previous use with light charring visible inside the chambers. The exterior of the corncob bowls remains structurally sound with natural variations in texture. Wood stems are secure. Plastic mouthpieces are intact without significant bite marks or cracks. Base label on one pipe is present and legible with minor edge wear. Generally well-preserved vintage condition.",
